@* I wasn't exactly sure what was meant by ReserveStudyFilters, but I took it to mean displaying the number of units and the study horizon, as well as the editform for the number of units. *@

@* The study horizon is a fixed value, so it cannot be edited *@
<h4 class="text-center">Study Horizon: @ReserveStudy.StudyHorizon Years</h4>
@* Displaying number of units the HOA oversees, with a button to change the number. *@
<p class="text-center mb-3">Number of Units: @Study.NumUnits <button class="btn btn-primary btn-sm ms-3" @onclick="ChangeNumUnits">Edit</button></p>
@* If the user is changing the number of units, displays a form tied to the research study object with an input for number of units *@
@if (changeNumUnits)
{
    <div class="container col-md-4">
        <EditForm model="Study" OnValidSubmit="HandleValidSubmitUnits">
            <label for="numUnits">Number of Units:</label>
            <InputNumber class="form-control" @bind-value="Study.NumUnits"></InputNumber>
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Submit</button>
        </EditForm>
    </div>
}

@code {
    // Study is passed in from the parent
    [Parameter]
    public ReserveStudy Study { get; set; } = new();
    // Event callback calls the associated parent method
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnValidSubmit { get; set; }
    // Bool tracking if the user wants to edit the number of units
    private bool changeNumUnits = false;
    // Called if the user clicks edit
    private void ChangeNumUnits()
    {
        changeNumUnits = true;
    }
    // Called if the user clicks submit on the editform, resets the bool and invokes the parent method to change nubmer of units
    private async Task HandleValidSubmitUnits()
    {
        changeNumUnits = false;
        await OnValidSubmit.InvokeAsync();
    }
}